---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="CV | Tanishk Tiwari"
  description="Curriculum Vitae of Tanishk Tiwari — AI systems researcher working on efficient LLM inference, mechanistic interpretability, and computational epigraphy."
>
  <div class="shell section">
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-end md:justify-between gap-6 pb-8 border-b border-line mb-10 no-print reveal">
      <div>
        <span class="section-num">CV</span>
        <h1 class="display-lg">Curriculum <span class="serif text-acid">Vitae.</span></h1>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-3">
        <button onclick="window.print()" class="btn btn-outline">Print</button>
        <a href="/cv/tanishk-tiwari-cv.pdf" download class="btn btn-primary">Download PDF</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <article class="paper-surface max-w-4xl mx-auto p-8 md:p-12 shadow-sm print:shadow-none print:border-none print:p-0">
      <header class="text-center border-b border-stone-300 pb-6 mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight" style="font-family: var(--font-display); color:#16202a;">Tanishk Tiwari</h2>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2" style="color:#444;">Software Engineering &amp; AI Systems Researcher · Efficient LLM Inference &amp; Mechanistic Interpretability</p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-xs mt-3" style="color:#555;">
          <span>New Delhi, India</span>
          <a href="mailto:t.high1945@gmail.com">t.high1945@gmail.com</a>
          <a href="https://horus84.github.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">horus84.github.io</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/horus84" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/horus84</a>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/Tanishk-Tiwari-2/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
          <a href="https://orcid.org/0009-0004-6482-4479" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ORCID</a>
        </div>
      </header>

      <section class="mb-8">
        <h3 class="cv-h">Education</h3>
        <div class="flex justify-between gap-4 text-sm">
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold" style="color:#16202a;">Delhi Skill and Entrepreneurship University</p>
            <p class="italic text-stone-600">B.Tech in Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning</p>
          </div>
          <div class="text-right text-stone-600 shrink-0">
            <p>New Delhi, India</p>
            <p>Expected 2028</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="cv-list mt-2">
          <li><strong>CGPA:</strong> 8.2/10. <strong>Honors:</strong> EACL 2026 Student Research Workshop Mentorship; ACL/NLP4DH 2026 Presenter (San Diego, USA).</li>
          <li><strong>Coursework:</strong> Data Structures and Algorithms, Probability and Statistics, Optimization, Machine Learning, Discrete Mathematics.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-8">
        <h3 class="cv-h">Research &amp; Systems Engineering Experience</h3>

        <div class="cv-entry">
          <div class="cv-entry-head">
            <div><p class="cv-role">Efficient LLM Inference and KV-Cache Compression</p><p class="cv-org">Independent Researcher · Remote</p></div>
            <p class="cv-date">2026 – Present</p>
          </div>
          <ul class="cv-list">
            <li>Developing a value-focused KV-cache compression framework to reduce memory footprint and latency during long-context LLM inference.</li>
            <li>Investigating adaptive low-rank representations, salient residual preservation, and compressed attention in PyTorch and Transformers.</li>
            <li>Benchmarking quality, memory, latency, throughput, perplexity, and long-context task performance; preparing for ACL Rolling Review.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="cv-entry">
          <div class="cv-entry-head">
            <div><p class="cv-role">Mechanistic Interpretability of Open-Weight LLMs</p><p class="cv-org">Independent Researcher · Remote</p></div>
            <p class="cv-date">2026 – Present</p>
          </div>
          <ul class="cv-list">
            <li>Built a modular interpretability probe suite for Qwen to study attention-head specialisation and activation patterns.</li>
            <li>Instrumented transformer forward passes with hooks to capture residual-stream activations and run activation-patching interventions.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="cv-entry">
          <div class="cv-entry-head">
            <div><p class="cv-role">Computational Analysis of Indus Sign Sequences</p><p class="cv-org">Independent Undergraduate Researcher · New Delhi</p></div>
            <p class="cv-date">2025 – 2026</p>
          </div>
          <ul class="cv-list">
            <li>Built and harmonised a corpus of 6,000+ Indus inscriptions for statistical and neural sequence analysis.</li>
            <li>Studied conditional entropy, PMI, positional regularity, directional asymmetry, HMM structure, and BiLSTM next-token prediction.</li>
            <li>Designed reversal and perturbation controls; published and presented at NLP4DH 2026 (co-located with ACL 2026) in San Diego.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="cv-entry">
          <div class="cv-entry-head">
            <div><p class="cv-role">Mixed-State Quantum Machine Learning and Trainability</p><p class="cv-org">Independent Researcher · Remote</p></div>
            <p class="cv-date">2026 – Present</p>
          </div>
          <ul class="cv-list">
            <li>Built mixed-state PyTorch and PennyLane experiments using amplitude damping and non-unitary operations.</li>
            <li>Measured gradient variance across circuit depths and noise settings to study parameterized quantum-circuit trainability and barren-plateau behaviour.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-8">
        <h3 class="cv-h">Publications &amp; Presentations</h3>
        <ul class="cv-list">
          <li><strong>Tiwari, T.</strong> (2026). <em>Statistical Structure in Indus Sign Sequences.</em> Proceedings of NLP4DH 2026, co-located with ACL 2026. Presented in San Diego, USA. <a href="https://aclanthology.org/2026.nlp4dh-1.28/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ACL Anthology</a></li>
          <li><strong>Tiwari, T.</strong> (2025). <em>An Empirical Refutation of Yajnadevam’s Devanagari-Based Decipherment of the Indus Script.</em> Independent research article. <a href="https://www.academia.edu/129821471/Empirical_Refutation_of_Yajnadevams_Devanagari_Based_Decipherment_of_the_Indus_Script" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Academia.edu</a></li>
          <li><strong>Tiwari, T.</strong> (2025). <em>Reading the Indus Anew.</em> Invited research lecture, Roja Muthiah Research Library, Chennai, India.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-8">
        <h3 class="cv-h">Selected Recognition</h3>
        <ul class="cv-list">
          <li><strong>Peer-Reviewed International Research Presentation (2026):</strong> Presented “Statistical Structure in Indus Sign Sequences” at NLP4DH 2026, co-located with ACL 2026, in San Diego, USA.</li>
          <li><strong>EACL Student Research Workshop Mentorship (2026):</strong> Selected for the EACL 2026 SRW pre-submission mentorship programme.</li>
          <li><strong>Invited Research Lecture (2025):</strong> Invited to present “Reading the Indus Anew” at the Roja Muthiah Research Library, Chennai.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h3 class="cv-h">Technical Skills</h3>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-3 text-sm" style="color:#333;">
          <p><strong style="color:#16202a;">Programming:</strong> Python, C++, Go, SQL, Bash</p>
          <p><strong style="color:#16202a;">ML / NLP:</strong> PyTorch, Hugging Face Transformers, scikit-learn, XGBoost</p>
          <p><strong style="color:#16202a;">Scientific:</strong> NumPy, pandas, SciPy, Optuna, PennyLane</p>
          <p><strong style="color:#16202a;">Tools:</strong> Git, Linux, Docker, REST APIs, Streamlit, LaTeX</p>
          <p class="sm:col-span-2"><strong style="color:#16202a;">Research areas:</strong> Efficient LLM inference, KV-cache compression, mechanistic interpretability, sequence modelling, statistical NLP, low-resource language processing</p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .cv-h {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #9c422c;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #d9cdc7;
    padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .cv-entry { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .cv-entry-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .cv-role { font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.92rem; color: #16202a; }
  .cv-org { font-size: 0.78rem; color: #666; font-style: italic; }
  .cv-date { font-size: 0.75rem; color: #666; white-space: nowrap; text-align: right; }
  .cv-list { list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.2rem; font-size: 0.82rem; color: #333; line-height: 1.65; }
  .cv-list li + li { margin-top: 0.3rem; }
  .cv-list a { color: #9c422c; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  @media print {
    .paper-surface { border: none !important; padding: 0 !important; max-width: none !important; }
  }
</style>
